WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.640
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B two.

2
00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:09.164
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.464 --> 00:00:17.388
Unit twenty-five: Inversion after Negative Adverbials. Today you will put negative adverbs first for formal emphasis.

4
00:00:17.688 --> 00:00:20.398
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.333 --> 00:00:24.787
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:26.605
Never.

7
00:00:27.617 --> 00:00:29.268
Never means at no time.

8
00:00:29.883 --> 00:00:31.337
Never have I seen it.

9
00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:34.544
Your turn. Say: Never.

10
00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:38.273
Never.

11
00:00:39.017 --> 00:00:39.902
Rarely.

12
00:00:40.917 --> 00:00:42.545
Rarely means not often.

13
00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:44.801
Rarely does she complain.

14
00:00:45.417 --> 00:00:47.953
Your turn. Say: Rarely.

15
00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:51.685
Rarely.

16
00:00:52.450 --> 00:00:53.428
Not only.

17
00:00:54.417 --> 00:00:57.426
Not only means used before a surprising addition.

18
00:00:58.017 --> 00:00:59.598
Not only did he win...

19
00:01:00.183 --> 00:01:02.882
Your turn. Say: Not only.

20
00:01:05.733 --> 00:01:06.676
Not only.

21
00:01:07.417 --> 00:01:08.220
Hardly.

22
00:01:09.217 --> 00:01:11.193
Hardly means almost not.

23
00:01:11.783 --> 00:01:13.214
Hardly had we sat...

24
00:01:13.817 --> 00:01:16.399
Your turn. Say: Hardly.

25
00:01:19.233 --> 00:01:20.037
Hardly.

26
00:01:20.783 --> 00:01:21.842
No sooner.

27
00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:25.186
No sooner means immediately before.

28
00:01:25.783 --> 00:01:27.458
No sooner had I left...

29
00:01:28.050 --> 00:01:30.842
Your turn. Say: No sooner.

30
00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:34.724
No sooner.

31
00:01:35.483 --> 00:01:36.333
Seldom.

32
00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:38.874
Seldom means not often.

33
00:01:39.483 --> 00:01:40.972
Seldom do we meet.

34
00:01:41.583 --> 00:01:43.794
Your turn. Say: Seldom.

35
00:01:46.633 --> 00:01:47.751
Seldom.

36
00:01:48.517 --> 00:01:49.634
Inversion.

37
00:01:50.650 --> 00:01:53.648
Inversion means reversing subject and auxiliary.

38
00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:55.750
Inversion is formal.

39
00:01:56.350 --> 00:01:58.956
Your turn. Say: Inversion.

40
00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:02.778
Inversion.

41
00:02:03.517 --> 00:02:04.564
Emphasis.

42
00:02:05.550 --> 00:02:07.631
Emphasis means extra strength.

43
00:02:08.217 --> 00:02:09.508
For emphasis.

44
00:02:10.117 --> 00:02:12.606
Your turn. Say: Emphasis.

45
00:02:15.467 --> 00:02:16.479
Emphasis.

46
00:02:17.267 --> 00:02:20.941
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:21.783 --> 00:02:25.350
Visal, say 'I have never seen such a view' starting with never.

48
00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:38.126
Never have I seen such a view. When a negative adverbial begins the sentence, the auxiliary comes before the subject. This is inversion, and it adds formal emphasis.

49
00:02:39.217 --> 00:02:40.914
Which adverbs trigger it?

50
00:02:42.017 --> 00:02:55.434
Never, rarely, seldom, hardly, no sooner, not only, under no circumstances. Rarely does she complain. Not only did he win, but he also broke the record.

51
00:02:56.550 --> 00:02:58.108
What about the pairs?

52
00:02:59.217 --> 00:03:11.290
Hardly had we sat down when the lights went out. No sooner had I left than it rained. Use when after hardly and than after no sooner. If there is no auxiliary, we add do, does or did.

53
00:03:12.433 --> 00:03:13.945
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:14.783 --> 00:03:20.092
Grammar focus: Inversion: negative adverbial plus auxiliary plus subject.

55
00:03:20.392 --> 00:03:21.706
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:22.417 --> 00:03:24.219
Never have I seen such a view.

57
00:03:25.117 --> 00:03:27.964
Not only did he win, but he also broke the record.

58
00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:31.523
Hardly had we sat down when the lights went out.

59
00:03:32.467 --> 00:03:40.602
Negative adverbial first + auxiliary + subject. Hardly… when; no sooner… than. Add do / does / did if there is no auxiliary.

60
00:03:41.350 --> 00:03:44.548
Be careful! Don't say: Never I have seen it.

61
00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:48.801
Say: Never have I seen it.

62
00:03:49.101 --> 00:03:50.486
Invert after never.

63
00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:54.335
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:55.133 --> 00:03:56.599
Formal Emphasis.

65
00:03:56.899 --> 00:03:59.177
Never have I seen such a beautiful view.

66
00:04:00.167 --> 00:04:02.410
Rarely does she complain about anything.

67
00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:06.433
Not only did he win, but he also broke the record.

68
00:04:07.433 --> 00:04:10.106
Hardly had we sat down when the lights went out.

69
00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:13.796
No sooner had I left than it started to rain.

70
00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:18.809
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:21.324
Never blank such a view.

72
00:04:21.624 --> 00:04:25.754
A, I have seen. B, have I seen. C, I saw have.

73
00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:31.636
The answer is B: have I seen.

74
00:04:32.783 --> 00:04:34.481
Rarely blank she complain.

75
00:04:34.781 --> 00:04:37.784
A, does. B, do. C, is.

76
00:04:41.333 --> 00:04:42.996
The answer is A: does.

77
00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:46.300
No sooner had I left blank it rained.

78
00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:49.325
A, when. B, than. C, as.

79
00:04:52.867 --> 00:04:54.634
The answer is B: than.

80
00:04:55.783 --> 00:04:58.329
Hardly had we sat blank the lights went out.

81
00:04:58.629 --> 00:05:00.982
A, when. B, than. C, then.

82
00:05:04.533 --> 00:05:05.999
The answer is A: when.

83
00:05:07.150 --> 00:05:09.765
According to the reading, who rarely complains?

84
00:05:10.065 --> 00:05:13.486
A, she. B, he. C, they.

85
00:05:17.033 --> 00:05:18.673
The answer is A: she.

86
00:05:19.867 --> 00:05:23.134
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:23.983 --> 00:05:27.527
Rewrite 'I have never seen such a beautiful place' beginning with 'Never'.

88
00:05:36.317 --> 00:05:37.620
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:48.911
Never have I seen such a beautiful place. I put never first, so I invert the subject and the auxiliary, have I. The sentence sounds more formal and emphatic.

90
00:05:49.211 --> 00:05:51.222
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:52.117 --> 00:05:58.983
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and inversion: negative adverbial plus auxiliary plus subject.

92
00:05:59.283 --> 00:06:04.571
Today's value is eloquence. Choose your words with care, and speak to persuade honestly.

93
00:06:04.871 --> 00:06:08.058
See you in Unit twenty-six. Goodbye!

94
00:06:08.358 --> 00:06:11.022
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

